          <tr align="left" valign="top"> 
            <td height="1088"> 
              <p> <font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><b>PMWATCH 
                - May 9, 2002 </b>-- For an institution that prides itself in 
                its intrepid and unapologetic quest for the truth, the US media 
                has displayed a remarkable degree of timidity and deference to 
                Israeli censors since the outbreak of the latest violence against 
                Palestinians in late March, 2002. A great deal of the truth has 
                been kept hidden from the eyes of journalists, and those who have 
                dared to deviate from the beaten path have had some severe punishment 
                meted out to them.</font><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> 
                </font> 
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> Below are 
                some press releases from the Committee to Protect Journalists. 
                </font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">Please press 
                upon the media the need to highlight to their readers and viewers 
                the extent to which the Israeli government is doing everything 
                it can to hamper the journalists in their quest to report on what 
                is taking place on the ground.</font>
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">Your letter 
                will be sent to:</font> 
